cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RiegoAzuay DSS, please cite this software release and the associated Land article."
title: "RiegoAzuay DSS"
version: "1.0.0"
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Ávila-Larrea"
    given-names: "Javier"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4056-4316"
  - family-names: "Hernández-Sancho"
    given-names: "Francesc"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9889-4131"
abstract: >-
  Bilingual evidence-aware decision-support prototype for parcel- and turn-level
  irrigation planning in community-managed irrigation systems of Azuay Province,
  Ecuador. The software combines a daily FAO-56 root-zone balance, turn-feasibility
  constraints, evidence provenance and readiness, bilingual reporting, and
  reproducibility controls.
keywords:
  - irrigation decision support
  - community irrigation
  - FAO-56
  - irrigation turns
  - evidence provenance
  - Ecuadorian Andes
